Z||000000||VISCERAL||08-13-99||01:57 PM||||HEY, I have an 1987 GT and a while ago I read about an autocrosser who showed up with those size tires. The tires didn't stick out of the body too much, as much as 245's. I have a koni coilover conversion w/eibach springs. So I can cut away at some of the spring perch to make room. My question is what kinda of offset different than stock can i use to accomadate it. I have to measure but I am pretty sure I could squeeze out another 1"-1 1/4" more room if I modify my spring perch. Stock offset is 35 or 40mm? Help!
Z||000001||Dale||08-14-99||01:26 PM||||Dont forget to factor in sidewall movement when cornering (about 1" to be on the safe side).  Yokahama AVS intermediate has 275/35/17 if your interested.  I have a set of these on my 71 datsun 510 (NICE TIRES) They match 235/40/17 highth wise perfect which I have on the front.
Z||000002||Dale||08-14-99||01:30 PM||||Forgot to mention!  If your going to have rims built, try Boyds.  I got mine for about $165 each through Les Schwab of all places  
